{:task
   #:seon.task{:kind :work,
    :id "seon.program/a-method-key-is-decoded-once",
    :plan
      "What exists: a method's dispatch value is encoded twice. `seon.program` stores {:dispatch (sedn/encode dispatch)}, and `seon.program/method-key` encodes [multi that-string] again. `remove-definition!` then reads the inner string back with clojure.core/read-string (program.clj:646), not `seon.edn/decode`. This is audit row C10's remnant: DUP-ROOT moved the outer decodes (program.clj:447, :705) onto seon.edn. Correct: the dispatch value is encoded once inside `method-key`, and every read goes through `seon.edn/decode`. Deletes: the inner encode and the read-string."},
 :references
   [{:symbol seon.program/method-key,
     :doc "A method's identity: [multi dispatch], printed.",
     :arglists ([multi dispatch]),
     :contract [:=> [:cat :qualified-symbol :string] :string]}
    {:symbol clojure.core/read-string,
     :summary "Reads one object from the string s.",
     :arglists ([s] [opts s])}
    {:symbol seon.edn/decode,
     :doc "The value `encode` printed.",
     :arglists ([s]),
     :contract [:=> [:cat :string] :any]}],
 :found
